# Flok multi-agent

Lead agent owns planning, commits, and PRs. Parallelize only independent streams. Prefer existing skills `multi-agent` / `swarm` for orchestration patterns — do not paste their full text here.

## Subagent map

| Work | Subagent |
|------|----------|
| Broad codebase map | `explore` / `repo-analyst` |
| Ambiguous design / multi-layer | `architect` then implement |
| API / DB / auth / tokens | `backend-engineer` |
| UI / OG / pages | `frontend-engineer` |
| After non-trivial change | `verifier` |
| Auth / secrets / seed / tokens | `security-auditor` then `verifier` |
| High-risk (OG rewrite, payments) | `verifier` + `red-team` |

## Ownership

- One file-ownership matrix per parallel wave; no two workers edit the same file.
- Subagent prompts are self-contained: objective, files, constraints, acceptance criteria.
- Never merge a PR without explicit user approval.
- Do not treat BRAIN or `reference/spx402/` as the product spec.
